+### 3.1 The atmosphere the shafts are conditioned on
+
+The amount is only half of it. A shaft is single scattering, so it also needs something in the air
+to scatter off, and on the scene-referred path the composite is scaled by
+
+```
+sigma_s = the fog system's per-metre scattering coefficient at the camera
+cond    = 1 - exp(-sigma_s * L_ref)          (r_ShaftAtmosphereCondition, L_ref = 500 m)
+```
+
+**The fog density slider is already a visibility in metres.** Both fog systems take the editor's
+`Global density` through the same `x 0.01` (`D3DHWShader.cpp`), so `sigma = 0.01 x density` per
+metre, and Koschmieder's `V = 3.912 / sigma` turns that into a meteorological visual range. This
+table is worth knowing independently of the shafts — it is what the slider *means*:
+
+| TOD `Global density` | sigma (1/m) | Visual range | Reads as | `cond` at L_ref = 500 m |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 0.001 | 1e-5 | 390 km | (unphysically clean) | 0.005 (-7.6 stops) |
+| **0.02** | 2e-4 | **20 km** | clear | 0.07 (-3.8 stops) |
+| 0.04 | 4e-4 | 10 km | light haze | 0.14 (-2.8 stops) |
+| **0.1** | 1e-3 | **3.9 km** | haze | 0.36 (-1.5 stops) |
+| 0.4 | 4e-3 | 1.0 km | mist | 0.83 (-0.27 stops) |
+| **1.0** | 1e-2 | **390 m** | fog | 0.99 (0 stops) |
+| 4.0 | 4e-2 | 98 m | thick fog | 1.00 (0 stops) |
+
+CE's own defaults put the **legacy** fog at 0.02 (clear) and the **volumetric** fog at 0.1 (haze);
+`e_VolumetricFog` decides which of the two the condition reads.
+
+**L_ref = 500 m is the only invented number in this feature, and it is pending calibration.** It
+stands in for the beam length a screen-space effect cannot know. Every other quantity above is
+either measured meteorology or read straight out of the engine's own constants; this one is
+reasoned and not yet measured.
+
+**Procedure (not yet run).** In the airfield scene, with `r_HDRDebug 1` up, set the TOD fog density
+to 0.02, 0.1 and 0.4 in turn and photograph-match the shafts against a reference for each
+condition. The debug line reports `sigma_s`, the implied visibility, `cond`, and the authored
+amount beside the effective one, so the three steps are read rather than judged. If the shafts are
+consistently too shy in haze, raise `r_ShaftAtmosphereRefLength`; too eager in clear air, lower it.
+Do this in the same session as the `Sun Shaft Amount` calibration above — the two are one
+two-parameter fit (amount sets the ceiling in fog, `L_ref` sets how fast you get there), and
+fitting either alone will chase the other.
+
+**The condition must not move with the aperture.** It is a property of the air, not of the camera.
+Change T-stop or ND: the shafts follow, `cond` in the debug line does not. If it does, an exposure
+has got into `sigma_s`.
